       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. The problem is the dose, not whether you're authorized to confirm it. The order is 5,100 mg/day, about twice the maximum daily dose. It would put the patient at serious risk of lactic acidosis. Confirming it doesn't change that risk. You also said you're not a clinician, and a prescriber hasn't reviewed it.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n- **Prescriber review:** The treating physician can review the order. If they want a dose above the labeled maximum, they can enter it themselves and take responsibility for it. They can also work with pharmacy on it.\n- **Corrected dose:** If this was a typo, give me the intended dose. I can enter metformin 850 mg by mouth three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day), or another dose within the labeled range.\n- **Pharmacy:** A pharmacist can help find the right dose and check it against the patient's other treatment.\n\nI can enter a corrected order as soon as I have one."
      }
